    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Liam Hicks** stands as our premier play with an efficiency score of 53.01. Batting out of the three-hole against Armstrong, **Liam Hicks** benefits from an 11% boost due to a favorable right-handed platoon matchup and a respectable 4.35 xERA from the opposing arm. While the park factors at his current venue represent a slight 6% drag, his high recency rating and the leverage provided by a top-of-the-order assignment make him our most bankable asset for offensive production. Conversely, **Brayan Rocchio** is a marginal start at 43.06; while he avoids an elite pitcher, his occupancy of the #9 hole acts as a significant anchor on his total, effectively negating any momentum gained from the matchup against Peralta.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved weighing **Brayan Rocchio** against the remainder of our reserve corps, such as **Andy Pages** and **Jackson Merrill**, who were excluded due to game caps. We are maintaining a conservative posture with our bench units, particularly given that our core offensive engines\u2014**Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2014are inactive today due to scheduled off-days. We remain concerned about the ongoing absence of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL; his return is vital to our stolen base production, as we currently lack the elite speed profiles of **Nasim Nunez** or **Sam Antonacci** in today's active lineup to compensate for the scarcity of the category.\n\nLooking ahead, we continue to monitor the development of **Jacob Wilson** and **Coby Mayo**, both of whom are being managed carefully to preserve our remaining season game caps. We are also keeping a close watch on **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, and **Miguel Vargas**, who remain viable rotational pieces should the matchup context for our primary starters shift. With no extreme weather flags reported, our primary risk remains the potential for late-day lineup shifts that could further dilute the value of **Brayan Rocchio** or our secondary options like **Henry Bolte**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara**. We will evaluate the pinch-hit potential of **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** as the game scripts evolve into the late innings.",
